ripple-manifest.json: @ripple-ui/svelte 0.8.0 manifest, vendored from qbtrix/ripple-iui#182
(branch feat/data-widgets) at a9ab3b37d9bf24d62fd14932aaf4da53cf1b9593, pending a release.
It is that commit's packages/svelte/static/manifest.json (generatedAt
2026-10-09T06:36:29.936Z, 197 widgets, upstream sha256
1716be4a8c6e61cc87bb6fdb93b98764e0b008a4d8e4d16c7e4ff31ed26030d8; an in-memory
buildManifest() at that commit matched it), with every widget's "example" removed.
The server never reads the examples, and one carries a sample Stripe-style key that
GitHub push protection refuses.

Refresh (once the data widgets ship in a release, use the release asset):
  gh release download -R qbtrix/ripple-iui --pattern manifest.json -D <dir>
  (until then: packages/svelte/static/manifest.json at the PR head, after
  `bun run build:manifest` if it is stale)
  python -I - <dir>/manifest.json ee/pocketpaw_ee/paw_bar/ripple-manifest.json <<'PY'
  import json, sys
  m = json.load(open(sys.argv[1], encoding="utf-8"))
  for w in m["widgets"]:
      w.pop("example", None)
  open(sys.argv[2], "w", encoding="utf-8").write(json.dumps(m, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False) + "\n")
  PY
then update this file and the pins in test_the_vendored_ripple_manifest_has_not_drifted
(tests/cloud/test_paw_bar_ripple_profile.py: _RIPPLE_MANIFEST_SHA256, version, count).
Once the manifest carries "illustration", drop ILLUSTRATION_WIDGET from card_spec.py
and the "illustration" not in every assertion in that drift test.
